 "notes": "The shared demo password is an example, so its value is not pinned: seed_password_hardcoded looks for a literal password value on the function (code or environment variable). Each seed_* check binds an email to its group and role within one user entry, in either field order; a design listing users under a per-group heading would fail these detail checks for all but the first user. A template passing the password in through a Secrets Manager secret fails seed_password_hardcoded because the prompt requires it in the seeding logic."
